WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.897
[PROBLEM STATEMENT] Welcome to SupplyGraph. In modern software engineering, software supply-chain attacks like Log4j, SolarWinds, and malicious npm lifecycle hooks have surged by over 600%.

00:00:11.897 --> 00:00:23.795
[PROBLEM STATEMENT] Traditional security tools like GitHub Dependabot, Snyk, or npm audit only perform flat, direct manifest lookups.

00:00:23.795 --> 00:00:35.692
[PROBLEM STATEMENT] This creates overwhelming alert fatigue—over 90% of reported CVEs are never actually reachable in application runtime code.

00:00:35.692 --> 00:00:47.590
[PROBLEM STATEMENT] Furthermore, when automated tools blindly bump package versions, they break production builds and critical backend APIs, while remaining completely blind to CI/CD runner exploits.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:01:00.663
[PROPOSED SOLUTION] To solve these fundamental flaws, we engineered SupplyGraph: an enterprise Application Security Posture Management, or ASPM platform.

00:01:00.663 --> 00:01:12.936
[PROPOSED SOLUTION] SupplyGraph unifies static dependency trees, multi-hop reachability graph algorithms, AST-guided surgical code remediation, runtime container sandboxing, and immutable blockchain attestation.

00:01:12.936 --> 00:01:25.210
[PROPOSED SOLUTION] Instead of isolated alerts, SupplyGraph correlates dependencies across npm, PyPI, Go, and GitHub Actions into actionable, verifiable security posture.

00:01:26.009 --> 00:01:35.461
[CORE FEATURES] SupplyGraph introduces four breakthrough capabilities:

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:44.913
